
==============================================================================
 1  THE METHOD, AND THE TWO ABSENCES
==============================================================================

  ==========================================================================
  a64data -- the artifact for "The AArch64 Data Path: NEON, Atomics and
  Ordering"
  ==========================================================================
  THE METHOD IS FORCED AND IT IS STATED FIRST:
    there is no AArch64 machine on this host, no AArch64 emulator and
    no AArch64 linker, so NOT ONE INSTRUCTION IN THIS COURSE HAS BEEN
    RUN, and there are NO TIMINGS anywhere in this file or on any of
    its five pages.

    The two neutral courses that own the PRINCIPLES both measured
    durations.  `simd` measured that a wider vector is 3.89x at 2 KiB
    and 1.14x at 24 MiB.  `smp` measured an uncontended `lock xadd` at
    2.54x a plain store and the contended one at 21.20x the floor.  The
    x86-64 sibling of THIS course measured 3.89x, 4.92x and 27.65x.

    NOT ONE OF THOSE HAS A COUNTERPART HERE, and the honest
    alternative to a number is not a smaller number.  Where a reader
    would expect a ratio on a page of this course, the page says what
    is missing instead.  Section 5 is where that bites hardest,
    because an INSTRUCTION COUNT is the measurement this course can
    make and it points in the OPPOSITE direction to the one a reader
    expects.

    The three labels, and the only honest treatment of a claim about
    a machine nobody in this file has run:

      MEASURED            an experiment on the compiler, the
                          assembler, the object file or the bytes.
                          One command reproduces it.
      MEASURED-ON-BYTES   a property of the emitted BYTES, read TWICE
                          -- by the decoder in this file and by
                          llvm-objdump-21 -- and the two readers are
                          compared word by word.
      QUOTED              a manual claim, with the document and the
                          section printed beside it, and never mixed
                          in with a measurement.

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
