    No copy of any of these documents was CONSULTED on this host.  The
    quotations carry document and section so they can be checked
    elsewhere, and the absence of the document here is a LIMIT and not
    a paraphrase.

  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
  THE TEST SUBJECT, AND THE RULE FOR BEING WRONG
  -------------------------------------------------------------------------
    The specifications are the ORACLE.  The compiler and the assembler
    are the TEST SUBJECT, and the architecture is the thing being
    described.  This is worth stating because the three are easy to
    confuse and the confusion is the most common error in this field:
    a refusal is a fact about an ASSEMBLER, a bit pattern is a fact
    about an ENCODING, and neither is a fact about a CPU.  Every
    disagreement between the two readers in this file is printed by
    name, in full, with the two texts side by side -- and every
    disagreement between this file and its own earlier drafts is
    filed as a RETRACTION in section 13, with the measurement that
    killed it and the general form it illustrates.  There are 27 of
    them and the rule is not "be careful".  It is: a claim that a
    reader cannot check is a claim the reader will believe, and a
    course about a machine nobody has run is MOSTLY such claims, so
    the ones that can be checked are the ones that carry the weight.

